<title>POLAND: Remak to lay off 50 employees.</title>
<headline>Remak to lay off 50 employees.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish engineering company Remak SA will lay off about 50 of its 570 employees to reduce the firm's costs, the company's deputy president said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Aleksandra Kowalska told Reuters that the reduction of the number of employees was likely to start having a positive effect on the firm's earnings in the fourth quarter of 1997, but declined to give details.</p>
<p>&quot;We have started laying off about 50 people -- it's connected with savings, we wanted to cut costs,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
